{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815178-looking-for-inspiration-and-sources-of-non-combat-conflict","id":815178,"title":"Looking for inspiration and sources of non-combat conflict!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T18:57:15-08:00","id":815178,"title":"Looking for inspiration and sources of non-combat conflict!","content":"I'm currently putting together a long scale Vampire game where I find the premise fairly interesting...but I'm not quite sure what the characters will be -doing-, and how to provide conflict during the game. Shortest version is that the game is Paris throughout the ages, set in 1814, 1914, and 2014. The time of things being more or less the same every night for centuries at a time is over; the Kindred society has to protect itself against the winds of change, with the years played as major flashpoints of extreme change both for the Kindred and the mortal society they hide from. In a lot of ways the game's set up to be very different from the regular setup; where most of the time shadowy Kindred conspiracies unknowingly shape static mortal society, the vampires of Paris have to deal with violent upheavals in nightly life that they don't really have any control over. The idea of playing up the Kindred's rigid society having to adapt or die is very appealing...but I'm not sure how I can translate the high concept into actual play that's also entertaining on a session-to-session basis.<br /> <br /> I'm not planning on the game to be very combat heavy, and while parts of the games will have access to the regular Machiavellian web of intrigue style political conflict that Vampire thrives on, at other times the All-Night Society is going to be far too busy just trying to survive the madness mortals are embroiled in. It's very clear that I'm going to have to rely -heavily- on the characters themselves and their ambitions to drive play, but in practice I'm still not sure what I can throw at the players while maintaining the feel of the game I'm shooting for. In all honesty, I've always struggled with how exactly I'm supposed to make Vampire work session-to-session, and this scenario in particular seems to eschew what structure the games normally have anyways!<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance, any help is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:30:22-08:00","id":815240,"title":"","content":"Have a general idea of where you want the game to go plotwise and incorporate your players Aspirations into it so they have a personal stake. Allow them to influence the course of the city through their actions but remember too that without extreme effort the grata of history will churn along as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:25:13-08:00","id":815473,"title":"","content":"Well, my immediate point of understanding is that you're setting up a Traditional/Conservaitve vampire faction versus a more changing sect. Elders tend to be static, yes, but those risen from torpor or newly Embraced can can deal with change. This is a classic Invictus/LeS versus Carthian/CoC city. The conflict? Stasis versus change. Arena? Social maneuvering, stealing herd and ghouls, undermining territories. <br /> <br /> Its all about the feeding grounds. Acomplishing your personal goals. Watching out for Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}